    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1952a2b_dae29ad8",
        "filename": "src/effects/imagefilters/SkMatrixConvolutionImageFilter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 959,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-25T15:34:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m sure this was pre-existing behavior, but I have to ask: When we are convolving alpha, we operate directly on premul colors? That\u0027s surprising to me.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 959,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 959,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "051e7cea29dd5947b63c15fdf8209c9172308772",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3d4d9c1e_fb72140c",
        "filename": "src/effects/imagefilters/SkMatrixConvolutionImageFilter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 959,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-25T16:40:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the SVG spec on feConvolveMatrix\u0027s preserveAlpha property, it says: \"A value of \"true\" indicates that the convolution will only apply to the color channels. In this case, the filter will temporarily unpremultiply the color component values and apply the kernel.\"\n\nNothing explicitly states that it does premul colors when alpha isn\u0027t preserved (corresponding to our `convolveAlpha \u003d true` case), but it would make sense that that is what it\u0027s implying.",
      "parentUuid": "b1952a2b_dae29ad8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 959,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 959,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "051e7cea29dd5947b63c15fdf8209c9172308772",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a22fddeb_63a8f582",
        "filename": "src/effects/imagefilters/SkMatrixConvolutionImageFilter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 1010,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-25T14:49:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PTAL at this updated shader, which packs the kernel into vec4s to not waste space when on std140.\n\nOn the raster backend on my workstation, this runs a 3x3 kernel (GM_matrixconvolution) in 10.5ms. If I provided a dedicated 3x3 shader, raster backend runs in 7.9ms. There wasn\u0027t any meaningful timing difference on my high-end GPU, but I\u0027m sure lower-end devices might see an improvement. For now, Rob and I agreed to leave it as 2 possible shaders and we can add the 3x3 option if regressions are reported.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 985,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1010,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "051e7cea29dd5947b63c15fdf8209c9172308772",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
